[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:10. Not for Jazz]
[00:00.740]Passage 10 | 文章十
[00:02.340]Not for jazz. | 不适合演奏爵士乐。
[00:05.560]We have an old musical instrument. | 我们有一件古老的乐器。
[00:09.795]It is called a clavichord. | 它被称为击弦古钢琴。
[00:12.510]It was made in Germany in 1681. | 它于1681年在德国制造。
[00:16.895]Our clavichord is kept in the living room. | 我们的击弦古钢琴放在客厅里。
[00:20.845]It has belonged to our family for a long time. | 它已经属于我们家很长时间了。
[00:25.100]The instrument was bought by my grandfather many years ago. | 这件乐器是多年前我祖父买的。
[00:30.955]Recently, it was damaged by a visitor. | 最近，它被一位访客损坏了。
[00:35.755]She tried to play jazz on it. | 她试图在上面演奏爵士乐。
[00:39.575]She struck the keys too hard and two of the strings were broken. | 她敲击琴键太用力，导致两根琴弦断裂了。
[00:45.535]My father was shocked. | 我父亲很震惊。
[00:48.655]Now we are not allowed to touch it. | 现在我们不被允许碰它。
[00:52.025]It is being repaired by a friend of my father's. | 它正在由我父亲的一位朋友修理。